/-!
# The long line table, `c² + a² ≤ 2468`

Source: `results/struct-lb-extend.md` §3.2 and §3.3, Theorem B, and the finite-range plan of
COD-269 part 1 (organize-archive b5cb45e). Below `n = 2137`, Hermite's bound `3 L⁴ ≤ 4 n²` gives
`L² ≤ 2466`, so every finite label is in the line case. This table extends the 844-line table to
all 2356 admissible directions `(c, a)` with `c² + a² ≤ 2468`. Each is covering on segments of
length at least `1/1176`. That is the bound of `results/struct-lb-contra.md` §3.2, item LN
(b5cb45e), whose worst line `(49, -9)` lies just outside this range.

The witnesses were chosen as for the 844-line table, by a greedy cover over the exact cells of
each line. Only the recorded segments enter the proof.

* `ctxT8b` : the 114 contexts that the witnesses use, with their cover masks.
* `lineGood_of_le_2468` : every admissible `(c, a)` with `c² + a² ≤ 2468` is good with `L = 1176`.
-/

